-- title:
--   Every element of ℚ̄_q lies over an algebraic number
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let `PadicAlgCl q` be the project's algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ (an algebraically closed, normed field extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$, algebraic over it). Write $\iota_q =$ [`padicEmbedding q`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L17) for the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra homomorphism $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` $\to$ `PadicAlgCl q` obtained by lifting the algebraic extension $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ into the algebraically closed field `PadicAlgCl q`. The theorem asserts: for every $\alpha \in$ `PadicAlgCl q` there exists $b \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $\alpha$ belongs to the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q}_q\bigl(\iota_q(b)\bigr)$, that is, the subfield of `PadicAlgCl q` generated over $\mathbb{Q}_q$ by the single element $\iota_q(b)$. Equivalently, `PadicAlgCl q` is the union of the subextensions of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ generated by images of algebraic numbers under $\iota_q$.
--
--   This is the standard consequence of Krasner's lemma and the density of $\mathbb{Q}$ in $\mathbb{Q}_q$: every finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside a fixed algebraic closure is generated by an algebraic number. It is the analytic input used by [`IntermediateField.exists_le_adjoin_padicEmbedding_image`](thm.html#IntermediateField.exists_le_adjoin_padicEmbedding_image), in the comparison of subextensions of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ with the topology of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ via the embedding $\iota_q$.
-- source:
